1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,425
A changing coast. A carved mountain. A forest that keeps growing.

2
00:00:04,425 --> 00:00:10,050
At low tide, the beach and reef tips are exposed. The trail is connected.

3
00:00:10,050 --> 00:00:13,050
Drag Tide amplitude from 2 to 4. At this low-tide phase, more shore is exposed.

4
00:00:13,050 --> 00:00:19,317
The water is rising. Watch the beach narrow around the same trees.

5
00:00:19,317 --> 00:00:22,033
The water has cut the dry connection. The trail is now disconnected.

6
00:00:22,033 --> 00:00:28,025
The same coast at high tide: exposed reef tips and the dry trail disappear.

7
00:00:28,025 --> 00:00:31,075
The tide is retreating. The trail is still waiting for a dry connection.

8
00:00:31,075 --> 00:00:38,042
The trail has reconnected. More reef tips emerge as the water retreats.

9
00:00:38,042 --> 00:00:42,042
Low tide restores the shoreline. Compare it with the high-water reference.

10
00:00:42,042 --> 00:00:48,391
Begin with solid terrain. There is no tunnel through this volume.

11
00:00:48,391 --> 00:00:56,266
Increase the cut radius. The opening widens through real remeshing.

12
00:00:56,266 --> 00:01:02,116
The tunnel is empty space beneath solid ground. Compare the same front face.

13
00:01:02,116 --> 00:01:08,058
Carve first, then add the pillar. The operation order brings solid material back.

14
00:01:08,058 --> 00:01:15,275
A local pocket changes the surface. Only 8 of 27 chunks were rebuilt.

15
00:01:15,275 --> 00:01:20,016
Start with the same 104 seeded trees. Tide and branch grammar stay fixed.

16
00:01:20,016 --> 00:01:23,025
Drag Growth rate from 0 to 2, then advance time. Reproduction stays at 1.

17
00:01:23,025 --> 00:01:30,108
Ecological time is advancing. Watch the original trees grow before seedlings appear.

18
00:01:30,108 --> 00:01:38,032
New seedlings are appearing. Existing trees also grow in size.

19
00:01:38,032 --> 00:01:44,033
232 living trees, 128 births and 0 deaths. Compare with the original stand.

20
00:01:44,033 --> 00:01:50,000
Three experiments. The same question: what changes when a rule changes?
